{
  // Items referenced by overlay additions that tarkov.dev does not serve yet.
  //
  // Every id here is a real BSG item template that `craftsAdd` / `seasonalPerks`
  // reference but that is absent from json.tarkov.dev in ALL served modes
  // (regular, pve, pvp-season), so an id-only reference would render as a raw
  // 24-hex string in consuming UIs. These entries carry the English
  // name/shortName/description so a consumer can resolve a display label today.
  //
  // Scope check before adding an entry: an id is only unresolvable if it is
  // missing from BOTH `{mode}/items` and `{mode}/tasks` -> `questItems`, AND has
  // no `"<id> Name"` key in the `{mode}/items_en` / `{mode}/tasks_en` translation
  // maps. Upstream serves questItems with placeholder `"<id> Name"` strings that
  // the _en bundles resolve, so an item can look nameless in the entity payload
  // yet still resolve correctly. Those do NOT belong here.
  //
  // Source: in-game EFT 1.1.0.0 seasonal capture (items.json template `_type: Item`
  // + locale_en.json `"<id> Name" / " ShortName" / " Description"` keys). English
  // only: tarkov.dev's locale system is the source of truth for every other
  // language, and these resolve normally there once upstream ingests them.
  //
  // Lifecycle: merge-by-id, same as craftsAdd - each entry becomes redundant the
  // moment tarkov.dev serves the item, and should then be deleted. Verify with
  // `npm run check-overrides` (reports itemsAdd entries that upstream now covers).

  // Moreman's audio tape #1  [craft product]
